   "title": "2-term lawmaker nominated to lead interior ministry",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/politics/20261123/2-term-lawmaker-nominated-to-lead-interior-ministry",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:27:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795429622.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "Rep. Han Jun-ho, tapped to lead the interior ministry, is a two-term lawmaker of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) who formerly worked as a news anchor. Han was elected as a lawmaker for the DPK in the 2020 general elections before winning his second term in the 2024 elections. \"As a two-term lawmaker and a former journalist, (Han) racked up legislative experience in various sectors, such as land, transport and artificial intelligence (AI),\" Lim Kwang-hyun, presidential chief of staff, said.",
   "summary_zh": "被任命领导内政部的韩俊浩议员，是执政的朝鲜民主劳动党（DPK）连任两届的议员，曾担任新闻主播。韩在2020年大选中当选为朝鲜民主劳动党议员，并在2024年选举中赢得第二个任期。总统首席秘书林光贤说：“作为连任两届的议员和前记者，（韩）在土地、交通、人工智能（AI）等多个领域积累了立法经验。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Rep. Han Jun-ho, tapped to lead the interior ministry, is a two-term lawmaker of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) who formerly worked as a news anchor. Born in 1974 in the southwestern city of Jeonju, Han graduated from Yonsei University with a degree in mathematics before joining local broadcaster MBC as a newscaster in 2003. He left MBC in 2018 and worked at the presidential office under then President Moon Jae-in as a communications official. Han was elected as a lawmaker for the DPK in the 2020 general elections before winning his second term in the 2024 elections. He currently serves as a ranking member of the parliamentary science, ICT, broadcasting and communications committee. \"As a two-term lawmaker and a former journalist, (Han) racked up legislative experience in various sectors, such as land, transport and artificial intelligence (AI),\" Lim Kwang-hyun, presidential chief of staff, said. \"He is expected to robustly secure public safety and inject vitality into region-led growth.\"",
